H=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P='additional_operad_skills_remaining';runpy.run_path(str(H/(P+'_synthesis06.py')));fs=json.loads((H/(P+'_preparation.json')).read_text())['files'];p=H/(P+'.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text())
def e(i,a,b):return {'path':fs[i]['path'],'sha256':fs[i]['sha256'],'lines':[a,b]}
def f(n,title,body,ev,action,validation='Full source review and stated mathematical reasoning; no retained workflow executed.',severity='medium'):return {'id':f'OPSKILL-F{n:03}','severity':severity,'title':title,'finding':body,'evidence':ev,'recommended_action':action,'validation':validation}
rows=[
f(54,'Retractions, transposes and complementary projectors are not involutions','The active-obstruction reference correctly distinguishes r composed u=id from involution, then names u/r, d0/d0-transpose and complementary projectors dual involution pairs. Retractions may be differently typed; projectors satisfy P squared=P, not identity, and a transpose is not a map inverse.',[e(189,33,47)],'Use section/retraction, transpose or complementary-projector terminology with declared domains. Reserve involution for an endomorphism whose square is identity.'),
f(55,'Regular degree alone does not imply Kesten--McKay spectral universality','The anti-skill reference requires the Kesten--McKay law for fixed-d regular graphs without random-ensemble or local-tree convergence assumptions. Disjoint unions of K4 are 3-regular of increasing size with unchanged atomic spectral masses 1/4 at 3 and 3/4 at -1.',[e(190,55,63)],'State a random regular or locally tree-like limit theorem with its hypotheses and distinguish finite empirical spectra from an asymptotic distribution.','CHECK-041 gives exact eigenvectors/eigenvalues and the disjoint-union sequence.'),
f(56,'Suggested modular normalization can overflow the stated native integer carrier','The formula ((lhs % m)+m)%m is mathematically valid for positive m but the addition can exceed a fixed signed integer range even when lhs and m are valid. For i64, m=MAX and lhs=MAX-1 gives intermediate 2*MAX-1.',[e(190,31,37)],'Use a checked/widened remainder operation or conditional addition only when the remainder is negative; reject zero modulus and document signed MIN/-1 behavior.','CHECK-040 uses exact integers; no native execution.'),
f(57,'Strict quotient improvement by an exact gauge CUT is impossible','Phi(c)=min_phi ||c-dphi||1 is invariant under c -> c-dpsi by translating phi. The reference nevertheless admits CUT exactly when Phi(c-dpsi)<Phi(c), so it rejects every genuine pure-gauge CUT. Reducing a representative norm or changing admitted cochains is a different operation and needs its own protected-query contract.',[e(198,24,31),e(203,66,76)],'Separate representative residual improvement from quotient obstruction. Use gauge invariance as a check; for obstruction reduction declare and verify a changed problem/carrier with lawful transport.','CHECK-037 proves equality on a triangle; the change-of-variable argument applies generally.','high'),
f(58,'Nonpositive change is mislabeled strict descent','The manifold reference labels Delta <=0 as Strict Descent, admitting stationary steps indefinitely. Strict rational decrease also needs a finite fuel or well-founded positive granularity for termination; the main WDP guide correctly adds fuel.',[e(193,10,16),e(219,89,98)],'Use <0 for strict improvement and a separate nonincrease condition; state bounded fuel/termination premise rather than infer it from the label.','CHECK-042 demonstrates a stationary accepted step.'),
f(59,'PFP strict-type and budget checks only test local examples and contain invalid-input acceptance','The PFP script cannot reject bool via isinstance(val,bool) and not isinstance(val,int), since Python bool is an int subclass. Missing/null/string answers also pass. Its mock ledger treats every non-None cost as valid, allowing negative, nonfinite and excessive charges; tests only exercise None. Hardcoded safe prompt and self-produced digests do not audit real prompt assembly or receipt replay.',[e(204,183,231),e(204,234,285)],'Use exact integer type plus complete candidate shape and domain validation, exact bounded nonnegative monetary fields, and production-owner tests with bound external problem/receipt inputs. Rename remaining examples as illustrations.','CHECK-039 and CHECK-043 mirror exact branches on synthetic inputs; no production or retained checker execution.','high'),
f(60,'Dual feasibility alone is mislabeled a complete optimality certificate','The simplicial reference lists d-transpose w=0 and infinity norm <=1 as the certificate for Phi. Those only establish feasibility/lower bounds. The zero vector always satisfies them, including a triangle with primal optimum one and dual value zero.',[e(198,24,31),e(170,32,43)],'Require primal feasibility and objective equality with the paired dual witness, including declared weights and exact arithmetic. Reuse the fuller solver-reference contract.','CHECK-038 gives a feasible zero dual with a positive gap.'),
f(61,'Live Genesis and S(n) reference tables disagree on the native frontier','One live reference says native S0--S6 and graph-free core; another assigns 22 native levels including simplex, Hodge and Regge content, and another uses a different 00--21 sealed Genesis table. These can be separate presentations/editions but the files do not bind a common translation and caller-specific frontier.',[e(192,9,17),e(199,19,30),e(200,19,39),e(201,7,32)],'Pin each table to an owner, carrier and edition and record explicit correspondence/noncorrespondence. Do not aggregate stage labels as additional native mathematical capacity.'),
f(62,'Pipeline and runtime verification success exceeds the actual predicates','Pipeline linter checks two files for tolerance/Fraction substrings and only warns about a potential probe defect. ROP checker accepts any nonempty two files. Neither verifies producer hashes, candidate bijection, monad laws, exceptions, atomic ledgers or probe firewall, yet terminals say invariants hold/firewall verified.',[e(206,18,26),e(207,34,71),e(215,17,26),e(216,12,45)],'Report exact structural/lexical checks, classify semantic obligations unavailable, and use pinned executable owner controls for each promised property.','Complete branch review establishes absence of the advertised checks.','high'),
f(63,'Test-isolation guidance and checker leave concurrency and population gaps','A shared --basetemp path can collide across concurrent pytest runs. The checker only creates scratch, omits nested engine/tests Python files and lacks the advertised POSIX absolute-path patterns; it never validates actual basetemp use or interpreter/isolation. The loadfile scheduling advice does not eliminate per-worker collection.',[e(217,22,32),e(218,13,34),e(218,67,104)],'Use a unique invocation-scoped basetemp, inventory the actual test owners recursively, report skipped populations and distinguish scheduling from collection/resource isolation. Narrow platform claims to observed environments.'),
f(64,'WDP checks cannot establish their displayed semantic invariants','CODA zero-gap check assigns both sides one without any feasible witnesses, and type separation assigns residual and defect the same Fraction. DDC code membership accepts an arbitrary substring/comment. Prime checks two counts of nine without comparing conjunct identities or evaluating any continuation predicate. The main skill correctly disclaims Rust/Lean replay, but scripts retain stronger success labels.',[e(219,124,136),e(223,143,188),e(224,125,145),e(225,56,77),e(225,100,116)],'Keep source nomenclature/count checks explicitly narrow and add owner-bound executable semantic checks only where needed; compare identities and preserve candidate/receipt bindings.'),
f(65,'Lean audit source scans are not AST inspection or complete theorem adequacy','The skill labels two rg scans as AST inspection. These can match comments, miss qualified/alternative declarations and cannot identify all transitive dependencies. The subsequent #print axioms is useful, but a standard axiom list alone does not verify the intended statement or rule out an explicit False premise.',[e(234,17,29),e(234,31,50)],'Treat rg as triage; retain complete elaborated statement, premises, source/toolchain pins and fresh #print axioms output per declaration. Distinguish conditional theorem validity from unconditional application claims.')]
d={x['id']:x for x in r['findings']};d.update({x['id']:x for x in rows});r['findings']=list(d.values())
vp=H/(P+'_checks06.json');v={'path':'dag/reviews/'+vp.name,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(vp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'description':'Seven independent in-memory exact/branch controls; no retained workflow invocation.'};r['validation']=[x for x in r['validation']if x['path']!=v['path']]+[v]
